<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Registrations of new cars in the UK rose a=
bout 13% to more than 90,000 in August, preliminary industry data shows.</p=
>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">If confirmed at 9am, when the final data i=
s issued, that would be the highest number for an August in eight years.</p=
>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The latest data from the Society of Motor =
Manufacturers and Traders is also expected to show that the market share of=
 battery electric vehicles rose to about 30% in August.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Yesterday, data from New AutoMotive showed=
 a 17.5% jump in overall new car registrations in August.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Elsewhere in the car sector, Volkswagen=E2=
=80=99s supervisory board has agreed to back a sweeping overhaul that will =
cut another 50,000 jobs and could lead to plant closures.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">VW announced last night that =E2=80=9Cafte=
r intense and constructive discussions=E2=80=9D the supervisory board had u=
nanimously approved the comprehensive future plan 2030 drawn up by the chie=
f executive, Oliver Blume.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The VW supervisory board includes employee=
 and shareholder representatives, and it was not clear that they would appr=
ove Blume=E2=80=99s plans.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">These cuts are on top of 50,000 already ag=
reed, as VW battles with competition from China, weak sales in Europe and a=
utomobile tariffs set by Donald Trump.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">After a week of bond market jitters, today=
 there will be some fresh insight into central bankers=E2=80=99 thinking, a=
nd the health of the UK and US economies.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Bank of England governor, Andrew Baile=
y, is due to speak in London this morning =E2=80=93 a day after his chief e=
conomist called for higher UK interest rates. Will Bailey =E2=80=93 among t=
he majority who voted to leave rates on hold in July =E2=80=93 push back?</=
p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Opponents of rate rises point out they hur=
t growth, and won=E2=80=99t tackle the oil supply shock caused by the Iran =
war.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">This afternoon the non-farm payroll will s=
how how many jobs the US added last month. In July the NFP showed a shock f=
all in employment =E2=80=93 economists expect a rebound in August, with for=
ecasts for about 56,000 new jobs.</p>
